kind: chat
exchanges:
    - answer:
        - attrs:
            content: Keep the two families as one enum with a `Recoverable` predicate rather than two error types — the scanner already threads one error value.
            id: 0198c1a0-0002-7000-8000-000000000201
          kind: prose
      completedAt: "2026-11-27T13:52:14Z"
      createdAt: "2026-11-27T13:52:00Z"
      error: ""
      id: 0198c1a0-0002-7000-8000-0000000000e1
      model: ""
      question:
        - attrs:
            content: …and keep recoverable separate from fatal?
            id: 0198c1a0-0002-7000-8000-000000000101
          kind: prose
      status: COMPLETE
      supportsEmbedding: true
      type: ASK
    - answer:
        - attrs:
            content: 'It doesn''t — the Tail case fails *structurally*, before any error value exists. Classify at the point the error is minted, behind the `Recoverable` predicate:'
            id: 0198c1a0-0002-7000-8000-000000000211
          kind: prose
        - attrs:
            id: 0198c1a0-0002-7000-8000-000000000212
            language: go
            source: |-
                func (s *Scanner) classify(err error) Severity {
                    if pe := asParseError(err); pe != nil && pe.Recoverable {
                        return SevRecoverable
                    }
                    return SevFatal // structural failures never carry pe
                }
          kind: code
        - attrs:
            cache:
                title: scanner.go § Tail scanner
            id: 0198c1a0-0002-7000-8000-000000000213
            uri: sieve://0198c1a0-0002-7000-8000-0000000000f1/0198c1a0-0002-7000-8000-0000000000f2
          kind: reference
      completedAt: "2026-11-27T13:58:31Z"
      createdAt: "2026-11-27T13:58:00Z"
      error: ""
      id: 0198c1a0-0002-7000-8000-0000000000e2
      model: ""
      question:
        - attrs:
            content: 'But the Tail scanner treats column-zero fences as fatal — doesn''t that contradict this? Here is the scanner as it stands:'
            id: 0198c1a0-0002-7000-8000-000000000111
          kind: prose
        - attrs:
            id: 0198c1a0-0002-7000-8000-000000000112
            language: go
            source: |-
                func (s *Scanner) tail(line string) bool {
                    trimmed := strings.TrimSpace(line) // defeats the col-0 guard
                    return fence.MatchString(trimmed)
                }
          kind: code
        - attrs:
            cache:
